            </options>
        </dialogue>
        <level>40</level>
    </npc>
    <npc id="d41b67ba-1546-4a84-9caa-50d42ea5dfa6">
        <name>Crosby</name>
        <title>Chamberlain</title>
        <type>CHAMBERLAIN</type>
        <gender>MAN</gender>
        <dialogue>
            <greeting>Welcome to Dion Castle. I keep the lord's accounts... and his patience. What do you need?</greeting>
            <options>
                <label>Who rules Dion?</label>
                <type>RESPONSE</type>
                <response>The clan that holds this castle, for now. Floran's harvest and Dion's markets fill its coffers, which is why so many covet it.</response>
            </options>
            <options>
                <label>How is a castle taken?</label>
                <type>RESPONSE</type>
                <response>By siege. Break the gates, reach the holy artifact and seal it. No peace is kept within these walls.</response>
            </options>
            <options>
                <label>Goodbye</label>
                <type>LEAVE</type>
            </options>
        </dialogue>
        <level>70</level>
    </npc>
    <npc id="764b97b5-9400-4f3c-b51f-9740b55fc60d">
        <name>Mercenary Manager Sanford</name>
        <title>Mercenary Manager</title>
        <type>GUARD</type>
        <gender>MAN</gender>
        <dialogue>
            <greeting>Swords for hire, posted where the lord needs them. Before a siege, every blade counts.</greeting>
            <options>
                <label>Where do your men fight?</label>
                <type>RESPONSE</type>
                <response>On the walls and in the plains. The Delu lizardmen raid the fields of Floran when the garrison looks away.</response>
            </options>
            <options>
                <label>Goodbye</label>
                <type>LEAVE</type>
            </options>
        </dialogue>
        <level>50</level>
    </npc>
    <npc id="7f930559-ca67-451f-88dd-6020fdf0458d">
        <name>Warehouse Keeper</name>
        <title>Dion</title>
        <type>WAREHOUSE_KEEPER</type>
        <gender>MAN</gender>
        <dialogue>
            <greeting>The castle stores: grain from Floran, arrows, pitch for the walls.</greeting>
            <options>
                <label>Can I store my belongings here?</label>
                <type>RESPONSE</type>
                <response>Castle stores are for the garrison. The warehouse of Dion, in town, serves travelers.</response>
            </options>
            <options>
                <label>Goodbye</label>
                <type>LEAVE</type>
            </options>
        </dialogue>
        <level>70</level>
    </npc>
    <npc id="29687d1d-82cf-4f22-a9af-daa6043c2ff7">
        <name>Gibbson</name>
        <title>Herald</title>
        <gender>MAN</gender>
        <dialogue>
            <greeting>Hear ye! Dion Castle stands in the name of its lord, and all who would challenge it must declare their siege!</greeting>
            <options>
                <label>Any news?</label>
                <type>RESPONSE</type>
                <response>The plains are restless: lizardmen to the south, strange eyes watching from the hills. And the Execution Grounds east of town are haunted again.</response>
            </options>
            <options>
                <label>Goodbye</label>
                <type>LEAVE</type>
            </options>
        </dialogue>
        <level>20</level>
    </npc>
    <npc id="1d0060d9-7de8-41d4-9a16-f8692d2bcc64">
        <name>Hodler</name>
        <title>Wyvern Manager</title>
        <gender>MAN</gender>
        <dialogue>
            <greeting>The lord's wyverns roost on the keep. Only the castle's lord and his knights may ride them.</greeting>
            <options>
                <label>Can I ride a wyvern?</label>
                <type>RESPONSE</type>
                <response>Not unless your clan holds this castle. Come back with a crown, friend.</response>
            </options>
            <options>
                <label>Goodbye</label>
                <type>LEAVE</type>
            </options>
        </dialogue>
        <level>50</level>
    </npc>
    <npc id="bf0a92ae-432d-47e3-8288-98bc631b0ba3">
        <name>Mass Gatekeeper</name>
        <title>Dion</title>
        <type>GATEKEEPER</type>
        <gender>WOMAN</gender>
        <dialogue>
            <greeting>Welcome to Dion Castle. The teleport circle north of the bridge leads back to the town of Dion.</greeting>
            <options>
                <label>Where else can I go?</label>
                <type>RESPONSE</type>
                <response>From Dion: Gludio by the north-west road, the Cruma Marshlands to the north, the Ruins of Despair to the west and the Execution Grounds to the east.</response>
            </options>
            <options>
                <label>Goodbye</label>
                <type>LEAVE</type>
            </options>
        </dialogue>
        <level>70</level>
    </npc>

    <!-- ===== Execution Grounds : gardiens du lieu d'exécution (PNJ des Execution Grounds de Lineage 2) ===== -->
    <npc id="e72933b2-d487-42e7-ba42-49773a84ca95">
        <name>Roderik</name>
        <title>Warden</title>
        <gender>MAN</gender>
        <dialogue>
            <greeting>These grounds belong to the dead now. We keep watch so that what was hanged here stays here.</greeting>
            <options>
                <label>What happened here?</label>
                <type>RESPONSE</type>
                <response>Dion executed its criminals on these grounds for a century. Their spirits never left: specters, ghouls, even the old headsman they call Guillotine.</response>
            </options>
            <options>
                <label>Is it safe?</label>
                <type>RESPONSE</type>
                <response>Near the portal, mostly. Past the gallows, nothing is. The hangman trees have taken a liking to the living.</response>
            </options>
            <options>
                <label>Goodbye</label>
                <type>LEAVE</type>
            </options>
        </dialogue>
        <level>40</level>
    </npc>
    <npc id="dab6ea7f-a69f-4da6-bd9b-71bcb980088f">
        <name>Endrigo</name>
        <title>Warden</title>
        <gender>MAN</gender>
        <dialogue>
            <greeting>Another hunter? Bring holy water, and do not linger after nightfall.</greeting>
            <options>
                <label>Who is Sir Calibus?</label>
                <type>RESPONSE</type>
                <response>A knight condemned for a crime he swore he never committed. His revenant still wanders the burial field, looking for his judges.</response>
            </options>
            <options>
                <label>Goodbye</label>
                <type>LEAVE</type>
            </options>
        </dialogue>
        <level>40</level>
    </npc>

    <!-- ===== Neutral Zone : PNJ de la Neutral Zone de Lineage 2 ===== -->
    <npc id="e9a4c850-1a05-4707-ae86-ab630282208e">
        <name>Prias</name>
        <title>Wanderer</title>
        <gender>MAN</gender>
        <dialogue>
            <greeting>The Neutral Zone: no kingdom claims it, so every beast does. Watch the moonstone beasts, they hunt in packs.</greeting>
            <options>
                <label>Why is it called neutral?</label>
                <type>RESPONSE</type>
                <response>Humans, elves and dark elves all walk these hills. By old treaty none may build here, so it stays wild.</response>
            </options>
            <options>
                <label>What lives here?</label>
                <type>RESPONSE</type>
                <response>Scavenger spiders and arachnid trackers in the woods, wererats along the river, and lycanthropes when the moon rises.</response>
            </options>
            <options>
                <label>Goodbye</label>
                <type>LEAVE</type>
            </options>
        </dialogue>
        <level>30</level>
    </npc>
</npcs>
